  "repo_truth": "Seven prior fresh reviews returned findings over earlier immutable subjects. The parent recorded remediations and now submits a 30-path subject that includes all seven prior dispatches and all seven remediation records. This dispatch states no conclusion about whether those findings are closed or whether the current subject is implementation-grade.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 30 manifest hashes, Python-ordinal order, aggregate, dispatch schema, HCM-2.2 handoff, and review ancestry before review.",
    "Review the complete documentation subject and all coupled status corrections, not merely prior findings.",
    "Independently validate all three Draft 2020-12 schemas, six duplicate-safe JSON artifacts, normalized selection equivalence, all runtime/control positives, semantic uniqueness/cross-record rules, links, fingerprints, and cross-document consistency.",
    "Return evidence-backed findings ordered Critical, Required, Optional, Nit with exact evidence, failure mode, smallest authority-preserving repair, and missing validation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, branch changes, preservation access, or user task hops.",
    "No Rust, Cargo, runtime tests, production assets, CLI/SDK implementation, HCM-2.2 reinterpretation, HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, or Phase 4 implementation.",
    "Do not accept remediation prose as a success conclusion; test every disposition independently."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke required skills, read AGENTS.md, and return BLOCKED on manifest or authority mismatch.",
    "Verify all seven prior review/remediation rounds independently, including selection normalization, persisted bytes, operation mappings, Phase 4 boundary, installed_complete recovery, timestamp identity, definition/context ordering, established-refusal persistence/replay, promotion current-definition closure, operation-family evidence refs, exact-ref/path schema boundaries, and atomic establishment authority.",
    "Replay every schema acceptance/rejection JSON-Pointer mutation and require the declared Draft 2020-12 result; independently probe inherited exact-ref/SemVer and normalized path boundaries.",
    "Verify promotion resolved_definitions equal the cited operation-context projection byte-for-byte and replay the regenerated promotion runtime/persisted-byte/control lineage.",
    "Verify every committed/refused result evidence ref uses its sole operation-discriminated transaction family and identical transaction ID, including schema rejection of both wrong-family promotion cases.",
    "Verify active_hold is only the logical projection of one established intent and that writing/established/pending intent crash states, byte-preserving moves, scratch cleanup, and all conflict states form an explicit acyclic persistence graph.",
    "Verify all positive/negative schema and semantic oracles, recovery/replay/currentness/retention rules, source/path/ref safety, classification ceiling, Phase 4 boundary, HCM-2.2 compatibility, and implementation-grade completeness without invented authority.",
    "Verify final-review/primary-commit inventory includes every prior dispatch/remediation artifact and excludes only the active dispatch.",
    "Return CLEAN only with zero Critical, Required, Optional, and Nit findings; otherwise CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repair."
  ],
